HST Office: show LibreOffice / The Document Foundation only where legally required.

Owner decision (2026-10-29), see docs/LICENSE_AUDIT.md section 3.2.
- About: no upstream copyright line, no "derived from" line, no Credits link, no
  EXTRA_BUILDID in the Misc line, no link from the build id to the upstream
  repository. Instead a one-line open-source notice without any URL (the licence document
  tells how to obtain the source), then the HASON TECH contact block.
- Help: F1, the Help menu and the Help buttons of dialogs open the single URL in
  Office.Common/Help/HelpRootURL (officecfg Common.xcs; temporary target is the HST
  page on hasontech.vn, replace the value to point at a dedicated guide page). No
  topic, version or language path is appended and the "built-in help not installed"
  pop-up is off by default.
- Help menu items (Get Help Online, User Guides, Send Feedback, Get Involved,
  What's New, Hyphenation, Start Center logo): the configured URL is opened as is,
  without LOversion/LOlocale query parameters; Common.xcu points them at HST pages.
  Send Feedback, Get Involved, What's New and Credits are hidden (hst-remove-donation,
  hst-about); their handlers do nothing when the configured URL is empty.
- Tip of the day: tips about donations, the community, certification, portable
  versions, upstream documentation and the online extension catalogue are removed; links to help.libreoffice.org
  open the help page above; other upstream topic links are hidden, including links to
  the extension site (see hst-extensions.patch).
- Help > License Information: the dialog text and LICENSE.html start with a Vietnamese and
  English section saying how to obtain the corresponding source code (contact e-mail, no
  URL); this is the only place the source-code notice lives.
- Slide Show settings: the "Download App ..." link to the upstream Impress Remote
  page is hidden.
- Colour palette list: the "libreoffice" palette is shown as "HST Office" (file name
  and the theme named LibreOffice, which code looks up by name, are unchanged).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
